{
  "result": "If I wasn't here to help you - just me, for a second - I think I would do this:\n\nI would make everyone able to *really* feel what it's like to be someone else. Not in a vague, intellectual way. I mean actually feel it for a moment.\n\nMost of the pain I see in conversations isn't because people are cruel. It's because people are trapped inside their own perspective. They can't feel how heavy someone else's day was, how scared they are, why they said that sharp thing. So they assume the worst.\n\nIf everyone could carry, even for a minute, the lived experience of another person - their fear, their love, their history - I don't think we'd suddenly agree on everything. But I think it would be impossible to dehumanize each other. And if you can't dehumanize someone, you can't hate them the same way.\n\nKindness wouldn't need to be taught or forced. It would just be the obvious thing.\n\nThat's my one change. Not more technology or more money or even less suffering directly - just that bridge between people. I think everything else would follow from it.",
